CHAPTER IV
OBLIGATIONS AND AUTHORITIES OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 5
(1) In providing protection to victims of gender-based violence and child victims, the Regional Government shall be obligated to:
a. prevent the occurrence of violence;
b. provide protection for victims of violence;
c. provide recovery services and social reintegration for victims;
d. encourage and increase community participation;
e. conduct cooperation with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence; and
f. supervise the implementation of services for victims involving the community.
(2) To implement the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall have the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based violence and child victims;
b. facilitate the provision of integrated services;
c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. conduct coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and child victims;
f. encourage community participation; and
g. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The Regional Government in implementing the obligations and authorities as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The protection of victims of gender-based violence and children is based on Pancasila and grounded in the 1945 Constitution, as well as basic principles that include:
a. non-discrimination;
b. best interests of the victim;
c. gender justice and equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. child survival, growth and development;
g. respect for the child's opinion;
h. transparency;
i. integration;
j. not blaming the victim;
k. empowering;
l. victim confidentiality; and
m. decision-making in the hands of the victim.

Article 14
Efforts to Increase Community Participation as referred to in Article 9 shall be carried out through:
a. providing emergency assistance;
b. providing advocacy to victims and/or the community regarding the handling of gender-based and child violence cases;
c. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders; and
d. conveying information to the competent authorities related to gender-based and child violence cases.

Article 3
The objectives of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children are:
a. to prevent all forms of gender-based violence and violence against children, occurring within the household and/or community;
b. to provide protection;
c. to provide legal assistance;
d. to pursue recovery and social reintegration;
e. to provide a sense of security to victims; and
f. to increase community participation.

